#sleela 2.5
material;
< Source-side canonical SLeeLa VM ISA registry. Numeric order is canonical. >
< Canonical opcode order follows the native enum exactly. >
< Runtime services (networking, files, sockets, threading, GC, cancellation, ownership, and teardown) are specified in /lib/vm/RUNTIME-SERVICES.md. GC is a runtime mechanism, not a hidden opcode. >
<< Runtime support: all canonical entries are dispatched by /impl/core. Unknown values are rejected and logged.
   (0..123 canonical; 124 OP_GC_HINT, 125 OP_RAN_MEM; 126..147 OP_IC_* idea-canvas;
   148 OP_VM_SELECT; 149 OP_MODIUM_SCAN; 150 OP_UI_CALL; 151 OP_SSEND;
   152 OP_CHECKCAST; 153 OP_INSTANCEOF; 154 OP_DUP2; 155 OP_OSLS_CALL;
   156..178 append-only math/native/Java-string/exception extensions;
   179..181 reserved Native IPC worker instructions; 182 OP_REF object references;
   183..184 Java UTF-16 String to legacy UTF-8 and run-time code-unit bridges.) >>
< Operating-system system calls (OP_OS_*, syntax 1.5) are a runtime-service family like sockets/files: a spawned process is a VM-local bounded handle. See /lib/vm/RUNTIME-SERVICES.md and /lib/operating-system/OS.md. >
